        "original_id": "3dd9bf59-fde6-589e-90ca-ae48c2dad59f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Gabriela Mistral, Alan Sillitoe\n- Awards: Nobel Prize in Literature\n- Groups: angry young men\n- Topics: lyric poetry, Latin American literature, English literature\n\nFacts:\n- In 1945, Gabriela Mistral became the first Latin American author to receive the Nobel Prize in Literature.\n- The Nobel Prize in Literature recognized Gabriela Mistral for lyric poetry inspired by powerful emotions that made her name a symbol of the idealistic aspirations of the Latin American world.\n- Alan Sillitoe was born on 4 March 1928 and died on 25 April 2010.\n- Alan Sillitoe was an English writer and was considered one of the so-called angry young men of the 1950s.\n- Alan Sillitoe disliked the angry young men label, as did most of the other writers to whom it was applied.",
